from functools import lru_cache


@lru_cache(maxsize=None)
def get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:
    if n == 0:
        return 0
    split_sum = (get_max_sum(n // 2) + get_max_sum(n // 3)
                 + get_max_sum(n // 4) + get_max_sum(n // 5))
    return max(split_sum, n)


assert get_max_sum(60) == 106
```

This is a memoized recursion over f(n) = max(f(n//2) + f(n//3) + f(n//4) + f(n//5), n). The earlier note calling it the coin-exchange recurrence was wrong; it's a plain memoized recursion. I traced the values by hand (f(12)=16, f(20)=28, f(30)=44, f(60)=44+28+18+16=106) but did not execute the code here.

